# Security & Governance

- Audit ledger: append-only, SHA-256 hash-chained. Serialize appends (advisory lock). No update/delete paths.
- At rest: AES-256-GCM. In transit: TLS 1.3. Keys on-box; use `cryptography` lib.
- PII choke-point: all LLM prompts pass through redaction. Test must fail if raw PII reaches a model.
- RBAC (app) + Postgres RLS (Supabase). High-value actions always human-gated.
- SHA-256 is hashing, not encryption. No custom ciphers. PQC deferred until bank clients demand it.
